/pub/data/weather/uk/climate/datasets/Tmean/date/England_SE_and_Central_S.txt</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[19]</strong> UK Government Cabinet Office. List of cities. https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-cities/list-of-cities-html</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[20]</strong> OpenWeatherMap. Current weather data API. https://openweathermap.org/current</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[21]</strong> Rey, S. J., &amp; Anselin, L. <code>PySAL</code>: Python spatial analysis library (<code>esda</code>, <code>libpysal</code>). https://pysal.org/</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[22]</strong> Hussain, S., &amp; Mahmud, I. (2019). pyMannKendall: A Python package for non-parametric Mann-Kendall trend analysis. <em>Journal of Open Source Software</em>, 4(39), 1556.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[23]</strong> Pedregosa, F., et al. (2011). Scikit-learn: Machine learning in Python. <em>Journal of Machine Learning Research</em>, 12, 2825-2830.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 10px 0;\"><strong>[24]</strong> Seabold, S., &amp; Perktold, J. (2010). Statsmodels: Econometric and statistical modeling with Python. <em>Proceedings of the 9th Python in Science Conference</em>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>","metadata":{}}]}